---
title: Creamy Homemade Baked Mac and Cheese
author: The Chunky Chef
source: https://www.thechunkychef.com/family-favorite-baked-mac-and-cheese/
tags: pasta, cheese, american, comfort food, kid-friendly, main course, side dish
servings: 10
cook time: 35 minutes
date added: 2026-09-12
---

Preheat oven to 325 degrees F and grease a #3 qt baking dish{} (9x13"). Set aside.

Bring a #large pot{} of salted water to a boil. When boiling, add @dried elbow pasta{1%lb} and cook ~{1%minute} less than the package directs for al dente. Drain and drizzle with a little bit of olive oil to keep from sticking.

While water is coming up to a boil, shred @medium cheddar cheese{4%cups} and @Gruyere cheese{2%cups} and toss together to mix, then divide into three piles. Approximately 3 cups for the sauce, 1 1/2 cups for the inner layer, and 1 1/2 cups for the topping.

Melt @unsalted butter{1/2%cup} in a #large saucepan{} over medium heat. Sprinkle in @all purpose flour{1/2%cup} and whisk to combine. Mixture will look like very wet sand. Cook for approximately ~{1%minute}, whisking often. Slowly pour in about 2 cups or so of the @half and half{2 1/2%cups}, while whisking constantly, until smooth. Slowly pour in the remaining half and half plus the @whole milk{1 1/2%cups}, while whisking constantly, until combined and smooth.

Continue to heat over medium heat, whisking very often, until thickened to a very thick consistency. It should almost be the consistency of a semi thinned out condensed soup.

Remove from the heat and stir in @salt{1/2%Tbsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, @paprika{1/4%tsp}, and 1 1/2 cups of the shredded cheeses, stirring to melt and combine. Stir in another 1 1/2 cups of cheese, and stir until completely melted and smooth.

In a #large mixing bowl{}, combine drained pasta with cheese sauce, stirring to combine fully. Pour half of the pasta mixture into the prepared baking dish. Top with 1 1/2 cups of shredded cheeses, then top that with the remaining pasta mixture.

Sprinkle the top with the last 1 1/2 cups of cheese and bake for ~{15%minutes}, until cheese is bubbly and lightly golden brown.
